WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.735
Another escalation in Vladimir

00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:03.503
Putin's war on Ukraine

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:05.238
for the first time in the 400

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:07.574
plus days since the invasion began.

00:00:07.574 --> 00:00:09.776
Civilian areas of Moscow

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:11.077
may have been targeted.

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:12.412
This plume of smoke

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:13.313
is the apparent

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:14.748
aftermath of Russia

00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:16.950
shooting down a drone, one of eight

00:00:17.217 --> 00:00:18.451
that their Ministry of Defense

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:22.188
says was stopped over the capital

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:24.057
That's why they brought

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:28.728
clear what remained

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:31.131
So far,

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:33.433
no deaths have been reported, though.

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:34.801
Drone debris has damaged

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.336
several buildings there.

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:37.470
Russia is blaming

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.972
Ukraine and its interior

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:41.041
ministry issued arrest warrants

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:43.309
for two senior Ukrainian commanders.

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:45.412
But an adviser for Ukraine's

00:00:45.412 --> 00:00:47.380
president issued this denial

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:48.281
saying, quote,

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:49.382
We enjoy watching

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:51.484
and predicting an increase in attacks.

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:52.585
But of course,

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:54.921
we have nothing to do directly with it.

00:00:55.422 --> 00:00:56.122
In the meantime,

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:56.890
Ukraine's capital

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:58.425
has been bombarded for days.

00:00:58.425 --> 00:01:00.894
The 17th aerial assault by Russia

00:01:01.194 --> 00:01:02.695
this month alone.

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:04.064
Let's take you now live to Kiev

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:05.565
and CNN's Fred Pleitgen.

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:06.032
And Fred,

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:08.168
you were learning that Vladimir Putin

00:01:08.168 --> 00:01:09.903
has now responded to these

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:11.905
alleged Ukrainian drone attacks

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:15.875
there as well.

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:16.543
He certainly has.

00:01:16.543 --> 00:01:17.310
And he also points

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:19.646
the finger of blame at Ukraine as well.

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:20.680
One of the other things

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.115
that was
that was very interesting about

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:23.049
that alleged attack

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:24.150
that happened early in the morning

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.385
hours is the Russians are very quick

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:26.186
to point out

00:01:26.186 --> 00:01:27.654
that these were actually substantial

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:29.055
unmanned aerial vehicles

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:29.823
that made their way

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:31.024
towards the Russian capital.

00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:32.992
They say these are fixed wing aircraft

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:34.561
and not some sort of octo copter.

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:36.129
That's a lot smaller than that.

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:36.996
They said of the eight

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:37.831
that they took down,

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:38.865
three of them were taken down

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:40.300
using electronic measures.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:41.601
But they also said that they actually

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.136
had to activate their air defenses

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:44.370
and use missiles

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.506
to shoot down the five others.

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:47.040
So certainly

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.575
this was a substantial attack,

00:01:48.575 --> 00:01:50.143
as the Russians put it, on Moscow.

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:52.245
Absolutely unprecedented.

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:53.847
Since the Russians started their full

00:01:53.847 --> 00:01:55.248
on invasion of Ukraine.

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:56.483
And you are absolutely right.

00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:57.550
Vladimir Putin,

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:58.852
seemingly quite angry,

00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:00.553
pointed the finger of blame

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:02.222
squarely at Kiev. Here's what he said.

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:06.693
Kiev chose the path of intimidation

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:07.827
of Russian citizens

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:10.196
and attacks on residential buildings.

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:12.532
It is a clear sign of terrorist activity.

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:14.601
The Moscow air defense system

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:16.035
worked satisfactorily.

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:17.470
However, there is still work

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:20.373
to be done to make it better

00:02:22.876 --> 00:02:23.943
So, as you've already

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:26.012
noted to Boris, the Ukrainians

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:27.447
issuing a denial earlier

00:02:27.447 --> 00:02:29.115
today, coming in the form of an adviser

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:30.650
to the presidential administration

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:31.417
here in Kiev, actually

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:32.719
pretty early on in the game,

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:33.853
where they did say

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:35.255
that they were happy

00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:37.223
that these drone attack had happened.

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:37.757
But they also said

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:40.193
they didn't have any direct involvement

00:02:40.193 --> 00:02:40.593
in it.

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:42.228
Nevertheless, as you can imagine,

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:43.062
the capital of Kiev

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:43.530
here, of course,

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:45.765
bracing for possible further attacks.

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:46.332
And, you know,

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:47.066
this comes after

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:49.269
what was really a very difficult night

00:02:49.269 --> 00:02:50.803
here in the Ukrainian capital.

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:53.072
Having witnessed this overnight,

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:54.641
there were waves of attacks

00:02:54.641 --> 00:02:55.308
by those

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:57.110
Iranian made shadow drones

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:58.711
that the Russians have been sending here

00:02:58.711 --> 00:02:59.979
for the past couple of months.

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:01.080
And it really was over

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.582
the course of several hours

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:04.050
that Ukrainian air defenses

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.185
were firing in the air

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:06.019
and we were hearing them

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:06.953
firing in the air

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:09.155
and hearing explosions of those unmanned

00:03:09.155 --> 00:03:10.190
aerial vehicles.

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:12.392
Being hit and falling to the ground.

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:13.893
There was one woman who was killed

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:15.228
in a large residential building.

00:03:15.228 --> 00:03:16.429
We were on site there

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:17.497
just a couple of hours ago,

00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:19.165
and there was substantial damage

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:19.832
to that building.

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:20.466
And again,

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:21.668
the Ukrainians, while saying

00:03:21.668 --> 00:03:22.435
they had nothing to do

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:23.603
with those attacks on Moscow,

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:25.271
certainly bracing for

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:26.806
what could be even worse to come.

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:30.543
Boris, again, a 17th attack focused on

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:32.712
Kiev by Russia just this month.

00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:34.080
Fred Pleitgen from Ukraine,

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.381
thank you so much.

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:35.848
And Jim,

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:36.649
we should note that

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:38.851
these drone attacks in Moscow,

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.620
some of them focused on

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:41.921
one of the most elite areas

00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:42.722
of the capital city,

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:45.024
not far from Vladimir Putin's residences,

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:46.192
elite and also civilian.

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:47.560
And that raises some important questions.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.295
We're joined now by retired Air Force

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:51.097
Colonel Cedric Leighton.

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:52.065
Good to have you on.

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:52.432
Let's look

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:53.900
at some of these attacks recently,

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.335
because one phenomenon

00:03:55.335 --> 00:03:55.868
we're seeing

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.070
are multiple attacks

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:57.770
in recent days

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:58.504
and weeks

00:03:58.504 --> 00:03:59.305
inside and,

00:03:59.305 --> 00:03:59.639
well,

00:03:59.639 --> 00:04:00.340
Russian controlled

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.108
areas of Ukraine down here,

00:04:02.108 --> 00:04:04.644
but also inside Russia itself, Kursk,

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:06.246
Belgorod, close to the border,

00:04:06.246 --> 00:04:07.146
but also in Moscow,

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:08.181
we have that

00:04:08.181 --> 00:04:09.515
strike on the Kremlin recently,

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:09.983
which the U.S.

00:04:09.983 --> 00:04:11.517
says low confidence

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:13.319
assessment was probably the Ukrainians.

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:15.488
Now we have these drones here

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:18.057
on the issue of civilian targets.

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:19.158
If that was indeed

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:20.660
the intentional target here,

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:22.161
what does that mean for Ukraine's war?

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:22.629
I mean, it certainly

00:04:22.629 --> 00:04:23.162
Russia has

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:24.497
come under enormous criticism

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:25.598
for directly and repeatedly

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:27.300
targeting civilians in Ukraine.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:28.201
Well, certainly, Jim,

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:30.403
if the Ukrainians are targeting

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:32.071
civilians deliberately,

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:33.573
that makes it a whole nother ballgame.

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:34.807
And that would be a very bad

00:04:34.807 --> 00:04:36.442
move on Ukraine's part,

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:38.278
because right now what they're enjoying

00:04:38.278 --> 00:04:40.079
is a lot of support from the West

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:42.248
because they are following basically

00:04:42.248 --> 00:04:43.416
or at least have until this point

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:44.617
followed the rules of war,

00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:45.985
the rules of armed conflict.

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:47.420
And that becomes really important

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:48.488
for Ukraine's war effort.

00:04:48.488 --> 00:04:50.823
They cannot afford to target civilians

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:52.091
and they shouldn't do so

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:54.093
by mistake either. Let's have a look.

00:04:54.093 --> 00:04:55.161
We know that the Ukrainians

00:04:55.161 --> 00:04:57.130
have been using drones prior

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:57.964
in this conflict.

00:04:57.964 --> 00:04:58.898
On military targets,

00:04:58.898 --> 00:04:59.732
including some

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:00.500
pretty old one here

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:01.901
going back to the seventies, been,

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:02.602
you know,

00:05:02.602 --> 00:05:03.303
a far cry

00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:03.903
from what we're seeing

00:05:03.903 --> 00:05:06.239
now, smaller, more mobile

00:05:06.239 --> 00:05:07.140
kinds of things.

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:08.541
Could that lead

00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:09.842
if this was Ukraine

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:11.444
and if the civilian areas were

00:05:11.444 --> 00:05:12.779
the deliberate target?

00:05:12.779 --> 00:05:15.181
Could that lead to disagreements with

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:16.849
the U.S.

00:05:16.849 --> 00:05:18.551
and NATO's partners?

00:05:18.551 --> 00:05:19.752
So one of the key things

00:05:19.752 --> 00:05:20.820
that the Ukrainians have done

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:21.854
is they've used weapons

00:05:21.854 --> 00:05:22.655
like this, like this

00:05:22.655 --> 00:05:24.324
t u one 41

00:05:24.324 --> 00:05:25.491
drone, which is based,

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:27.827
like you said, on Soviet

00:05:27.827 --> 00:05:28.861
model that they've had

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:30.897
for many, many years.

00:05:30.897 --> 00:05:34.167
This the idea here is that they are using

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:36.969
their own systems to target Russia

00:05:37.704 --> 00:05:39.972
They are not using Western systems.

00:05:39.972 --> 00:05:41.574
They are not using U.S. systems.

00:05:41.574 --> 00:05:42.241
And they're doing that

00:05:42.241 --> 00:05:43.343
deliberately because the US

00:05:43.343 --> 00:05:44.344
has very specifically

00:05:44.344 --> 00:05:45.078
told them

00:05:45.078 --> 00:05:46.879
not to use Western system

00:05:46.879 --> 00:05:49.115
Notably, they use a Ukrainian

00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:50.083
manufactured missile

00:05:50.083 --> 00:05:52.552
to strike the Russian Moscow

00:05:52.552 --> 00:05:53.820
flagship of the Black Sea fleet

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:54.220
going back

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:56.189
to the early stages of the war.

00:05:56.189 --> 00:05:58.091
But before we go, let's look back again

00:05:58.091 --> 00:06:00.059
at all
these sites that have taken hits

00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:02.695
by Ukrainian forces in recent days.

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:05.131
This just in the last 24 hours here.

00:06:05.131 --> 00:06:06.933
Given the anticipation

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:08.701
of a Ukrainian ground

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:10.336
offensive to take back

00:06:10.336 --> 00:06:11.738
some of this Russian control

00:06:11.738 --> 00:06:13.473
territory down here.

00:06:13.473 --> 00:06:14.874
If you were planning this attack,

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:15.875
might you do this

00:06:15.875 --> 00:06:17.744
to create some fear uncertainty

00:06:17.744 --> 00:06:19.712
on the other side prior? Absolutely.

00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:21.047
And the reason for that is, you know,

00:06:21.047 --> 00:06:22.148
if your main target area

00:06:22.148 --> 00:06:23.950
is all of this down here,

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:25.284
then what you want to do

00:06:25.284 --> 00:06:26.519
is you want to make sure

00:06:26.519 --> 00:06:26.853
that you're

00:06:26.853 --> 00:06:27.453
keeping people

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:28.688
guessing that you could also

00:06:28.688 --> 00:06:30.690
potentially attack in this area

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:33.860
and especially right here in in Belgorod,

00:06:34.327 --> 00:06:35.962
because that area

00:06:35.962 --> 00:06:38.331
is not only close to Ukraine,

00:06:38.331 --> 00:06:38.998
but it has a

00:06:38.998 --> 00:06:41.067
is a major staging area for the Russians.

00:06:41.067 --> 00:06:42.301
And if they attack there,

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:43.569
that would be a legitimate target

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:45.571
for the Ukrainians to attack.

00:06:45.571 --> 00:06:46.172
In addition

00:06:46.172 --> 00:06:47.907
to all of these areas right here,

00:06:47.907 --> 00:06:48.775
I remember

00:06:48.775 --> 00:06:50.176
in the first day of the invasion

00:06:50.176 --> 00:06:51.310
watching Russian tanks,

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:52.512
we had our Fred Pleitgen up there

00:06:52.512 --> 00:06:52.979
on the border

00:06:52.979 --> 00:06:54.480
action and drive across the border

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:55.681
into Ukraine for the war.

00:06:55.681 --> 00:06:56.549
Senator Clinton, thanks so.

